<article class="env-lemma" id="0C5D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C5D">Lemma <span data-tag="0C5D">53.20.8</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $\{ U_ i \to X\} $ be an étale covering. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is at-worst-nodal of relative dimension $1$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
each $U_ i \to S$ is at-worst-nodal of relative dimension $1$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In other words, being at-worst-nodal of relative dimension $1$ is étale local on the source. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      One direction we have seen in Lemma <a href="/tag/0C5C" data-tag="0C5C">53.20.6</a>. For the other direction, observe that being locally of finite presentation, flat, or to have relative dimension $1$ is étale local on the source (Descent, Lemmas <a href="/tag/036N" data-tag="036N">35.28.1</a>, <a href="/tag/036K" data-tag="036K">35.27.1</a>, and <a href="/tag/04NL" data-tag="04NL">35.33.8</a>). Taking fibres we reduce to the case where $S$ is the spectrum of a field. In this case the result follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0C57" data-tag="0C57">53.19.13</a> (and the fact that being smooth is étale local on the source by Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/036U" data-tag="036U">35.30.1</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>